What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/state
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Current smart-card controller state.  The possible values are
		"no-card", "inactive", "wait-atr", "read-atr" and "ready".

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/card_present
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read-only cached card-detect state maintained by the driver state
		machine. One means the last observed state was present. Use
		hardware_status while the port is open to distinguish this cache
		from the controller's current conditioned detection signal.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/hardware_status
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read-only, driver-locked snapshot of non-consuming SCI status and
		configuration. The space-separated key=value fields report cached
		and live controller card presence, state, ISO7816 flags, CR0/CR1,
		clock/ETU/baud/debounce configuration, FIFO counts, IMSC/RIS/MIS
		and SYNCACT. Hardware presence is SYNCACT bit 10 after the configured
		detect inversion; it is not an independent socket voltage reading.
		The read returns EHOSTDOWN while the TTY is closed or PM-blocked.
		It never enables clocks, changes card power or polarity, refreshes
		the software cache, acknowledges interrupts, or reads DATA/ATR
		contents. Reading this attribute cannot activate or recover a card.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/tx_active
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read-only transmit transaction state.  One means that the driver is
		feeding, or has paused while feeding, the transmit FIFO.  Hardware may
		finish draining after the driver performs the original early
		receive-direction hand-off.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/atr
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Last answer-to-reset captured by the controller driver.  The first
		field is the byte count followed by hexadecimal bytes.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/atr_protocol
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Protocol parsed from the current ATR, formatted as "T=N", or
		"unknown" before a protocol has been parsed.  An ATR without TD
		implicitly selects T=0 when complete.  A parsed TD is visible before
		the remaining ATR is validated; use state to determine readiness.
		A successful enabled TIOCSISO7816 reconfiguration after ATR/PPS
		updates this value to the userspace-selected working protocol.
		The driver rounds the complete Fi/Di module-clock ratio to the
		nearest hardware clock count when configuring the bit timing.

