What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/recoveries
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Monotonic driver counters used to diagnose ISO/IEC 7816 transport,
		ATR and interrupt failures without enabling verbose interrupt logs.
		TX errors and RX overruns are reported through the standard TTY error
		path; they do not automatically FINISH or reactivate the card.
		A transmit re-kick is a serial-core start request received while a
		transaction is already active.  Short hand-offs occur after the first
		FIFO fill; refill hand-offs occur after a later TX-tide interrupt or
		re-kick.  A drain append is a fragmented TTY write appended while the
		previous hand-off still has bytes in the hardware TX FIFO.  The total
		hand-off count is the sum of the short and refill classes.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/last_irq_status
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Last non-zero masked interrupt status observed by the driver, in
		hexadecimal.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/recover
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Write-only recovery control.  Writing "1" while the port is open
		stops transmit, clears stale FIFO and interrupt state, and restores
		receive direction.  If ISO7816 is enabled, a present card is
		reactivated.  Normal transmit completion never invokes this full recovery.
		Normal transactions clear stale FIFO state at their start and switch to
		receive direction as soon as the last software byte enters the hardware
		transmit FIFO. Only a refill after the initial FIFO fill repeats the
		original RX-FIFO clear before that switch; a short command does not clear RX
		twice.
